urant Manager\nTo: Beatriz Okafor\n\nI reviewed the ticket history. The soup was entered under your table by mistake. The chicken belonged to table 14, whose guests also reported a delay, but their order is unrelated to your account. Your risotto ticket was delayed after the first dish was voided. I am sorry that the meal was not served promptly or at the proper temperature. The restaurant will brief the team on checking table numbers before food leaves the pass.\n\nFrom: Beatriz Okafor\nTo: Bracken Quay Hotel Restaurant Manager\n\nThat is at least an answer, although “brief the team” sounds like the sort of promise that disappears by tomorrow. I am still angry that I had to chase you to get a response. Please confirm that the written apology will come from the manager, not an automated message. Again, I have not asked for compensation. My complaint is about the service and the lack of a timely response, not a demand for cash. I want an actual person to acknowledge it.\n\nFrom: Bracken Quay Hotel Guest Services\nTo: Beatriz Okafor\n\nConfirmed: the restaurant manager has sent the apology in this thread. We have also recorded your request for a written explanation. Your room charge remains unchanged because you did not request a room refund or a discount. We are sorry the stay fell short of your expectations, and we will not send the survey invitation you mentioned.\n\nFrom: Beatriz Okafor\nTo: Bracken Quay Hotel Guest Services\n\nI have received the apology. I still think the hotel handled this badly, and I expect you to make sure future guests are not served a dish ordered by somebody else. Please do not confuse my request for an explanation with a request for a refund. I have said plainly that I am not asking for money back.",
