g, but it made an already irritating evening worse.\n\nFor clarity, the party seated ahead of us had a blue scarf and ordered steak. The other party near the window had a stroller and asked for a high chair. Neither detail concerns our order. Our table was number 22, and the receipt number ends in 681. The server called my friend “the trout guest” when checking the plate, so the kitchen had the information it needed. The ticket printout may show a second stew because that is what was first entered, but it does not mean we asked for two stews.\n\nI understand that restaurants get busy. That does not excuse serving food that was ordered incorrectly, then making a guest wait for the replacement dish until everyone else had finished. Please review the kitchen ticket and speak to the person who served our table. I would like a reply stating what you found, not a copy of your general service policy. I do not need another survey link, and I do not want a reservation offer for another night. A direct explanation from the manager is what I am requesting.\n\nI am submitting this form because the server said the manager might not see a verbal complaint. Please confirm that this has reached the manager. I am angry, but I have tried to make the facts clear: we were two guests, one trout was ordered, it came late and cold, and the initial duplicate stew was not what we ordered. Please address those points without mixing in the other guests’ steak, stroller, or seating details.",
